posts.body:
Since this forum is closing down, unfortunately share I will share my fondest memory here. It was when
@ct_bolt
made a plugin for me to help toggle on and off a Displayed Variable for my game Path of the Martyrs. Whenever the variable was adjusted the plugin would trigger and briefly show the variable change then turn off. The fact he did this help another dev out was cool. So what are some of your fondest memories here?

I don't think I have any fond memories, but I think it was a funny time here when
@TESTOSTERONE
was actively pushing their game!

You darn Degica Spy
@TRIDIUM
how dare you keep the truth from us?

Advent calendars for sure.
@Avery
started it several years ago, and then more and more people joined in. Aside from family, it was my favorite time of Christmas. My only regret is that I never had the skills to contribute anything in return.

The amount of resources that the community uploaded here is astounding. I used a good amount of those. I found a lot of tutorials and help on here as well like how to add steam achievements to your game. And I enjoyed connecting with some cool people on here.
I got to work with
@Puffer
,
@Miss Nile
,
@Low
,
@rpgLord69
,
@Plueschkatze
and many others. Each one is very skilled, creative and talented.
I had a really fun time chatting with
@Dalph
and
@TRIDIUM
too and they helped a great deal to make game development fun as I was working on Wind Ryder.
Christmas jam that we organized and had so many members participate in was great.
I look forward to migrating to our new home.

That time
@Ms Littlefish
said she wud flirt wid me, I guess?

Well dang
@alice_gristle
it’s a shame you missed the opportunity to have margaritas with me last night. I think the waitress fell in love with me.

I see
@alice_gristle
and
@Ms Littlefish
are openly flirting. XP
@AquaEcho
I learned “true” is on, “false” is off and && is and. That is the extent of my Jabascript knowledge
@TESTOSTERONE
It is astonishing how many requests there for RPG Maker. Also the Christmas Jam was fun, maybe another is in order once you find your new landing pad.
@EntangledPear
This forum definitely dug me out of a hole more times than I can count.
@Ryisunique
Shootimg the breeze here was definitely nice.
@TeiRaven
this forum definitely feels like a small coffee shop run by a couple who love people.
@ShadowDragon
this forum was the hub for a lot of talented and generous people.
@Indinera
The staff were helpful and always gave a great explanation on how things worked.

Honestly, every interaction I had with those that have become my friends means a lot to me. Without this place, I wouldn't have met so many great people like
@ATT_Turan
or
@RCXGaming
or
@Ms Littlefish
to name a few.
Beyond that, there was just the joy of popping up and possibly being able to help someone. I'm gonna miss this place a lot.
